{"key":"u13-apphy1-mcq-008-v2","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"B","working":"The increase in gravitational potential energy near Earth's surface is calculated as ΔUg = mgΔy = (60 kg)(10 m/s²)(15 m) = 9000 J.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"3.3","required_units":[3],"difficulty":"Easy"},"usage":{"inputTokens":6571,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":6571,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":478,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":139,"reasoningTokens":339},"totalTokens":7049,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":339,"promptTokenCount":6571,"candidatesTokenCount":139,"totalTokenCount":7049,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":6571}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":139}]},"reasoningTokens":339,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":4057,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphy1-mcq-008-v2","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"B","working":"Use the near-surface gravitational potential energy change formula: ΔU_g = mgΔy. With m = 60 kg, g = 10 m/s², and Δy = 15 m, ΔU_g = (60)(10)(15) = 9000 J. This matches choice B.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"3.3 Potential Energy","required_units":[3],"difficulty":"Easy"},"usage":{"inputTokens":6259,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":115,"cacheReadTokens":6144},"outputTokens":398,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":147,"reasoningTokens":251},"totalTokens":6657,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":6259,"completion_tokens":398,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":6144,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":115,"total_tokens":6657,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":6144},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":251}},"reasoningTokens":251,"cachedInputTokens":6144},"ms":4558,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphy1-mcq-019-v3","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"A","working":"The classic tablecloth pull is an example of Newton's first law (inertia). The vase tends to remain at rest due to its inertia, and because the pull is quick, the frictional force from the cloth acts over a very brief time, giving a negligible change in momentum.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"2.4","required_units":[2],"difficulty":"Easy"},"usage":{"inputTokens":6584,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":6584,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":552,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":149,"reasoningTokens":403},"totalTokens":7136,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":403,"promptTokenCount":6584,"candidatesTokenCount":149,"totalTokenCount":7136,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":6584}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":149}]},"reasoningTokens":403,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":5204,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphy1-mcq-032-v3","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"C","working":"The maximum static friction force is $F_{f,s,\\text{max}} = \\mu_s F_n = 0.50 \\times (10\\text{ kg})(10\\text{ m/s}^2) = 50\\text{ N}$. Since the applied push of $35\\text{ N} \\le 50\\text{ N}$, the cabinet remains in static equilibrium. By Newton's first law, the static friction force equals the applied force: $F_{f,s} = 35\\text{ N}$.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"2.7","required_units":[2],"difficulty":"Medium"},"usage":{"inputTokens":6618,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":6618,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":742,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":218,"reasoningTokens":524},"totalTokens":7360,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":524,"promptTokenCount":6618,"candidatesTokenCount":218,"totalTokenCount":7360,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":6618}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":218}]},"reasoningTokens":524,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":5824,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphy1-mcq-032-v3","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"C","working":"The cabinet remains at rest, so net force is zero. Static friction matches the applied horizontal push as long as it does not exceed its maximum. Maximum static friction is μs mg = 0.50 × 10 × 10 = 50 N. Since 35 N is below this, the friction force is 35 N.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"2.7","required_units":[2],"difficulty":"Easy"},"usage":{"inputTokens":6300,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":28,"cacheReadTokens":6272},"outputTokens":518,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":150,"reasoningTokens":368},"totalTokens":6818,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":6300,"completion_tokens":518,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":6272,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":28,"total_tokens":6818,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":6272},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":368}},"reasoningTokens":368,"cachedInputTokens":6272},"ms":6045,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphy1-mcq-004-v3","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"D","working":"According to Newton's third law, if object A (Earth) exerts a force on object B (the Moon), object B exerts an equal and opposite force on object A. Therefore, the third-law partner of Earth's gravitational pull on the Moon is the Moon's gravitational pull on Earth.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"2.3","required_units":[2],"difficulty":"Easy"},"usage":{"inputTokens":6579,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":6579,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":528,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":156,"reasoningTokens":372},"totalTokens":7107,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":372,"promptTokenCount":6579,"candidatesTokenCount":156,"totalTokenCount":7107,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":6579}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":156}]},"reasoningTokens":372,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":14573,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphy1-mcq-034-v1","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"C","working":"At the bottom of the dip, the net centripetal acceleration is upward: a_c = v^2/r = 15^2 / 30 = 7.5 m/s^2. By Newton's second law, F_N - mg = m*a_c, so F_N = m(g + a_c) = 1200(10 + 7.5) = 21000 N.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"2.9","required_units":[2],"difficulty":"Medium"},"usage":{"inputTokens":6603,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":6603,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":563,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":196,"reasoningTokens":367},"totalTokens":7166,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":367,"promptTokenCount":6603,"candidatesTokenCount":196,"totalTokenCount":7166,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":6603}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":196}]},"reasoningTokens":367,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":6843,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphy1-mcq-034-v1","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"C","working":"At the lowest point, the net force toward the center is N - mg = mv²/r. So N = m(g + v²/r) = 1200(10 + 225/30) = 1200(17.5) = 21000 N.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"2.9 Circular Motion","required_units":[2],"difficulty":"Medium"},"usage":{"inputTokens":6284,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":12,"cacheReadTokens":6272},"outputTokens":615,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":141,"reasoningTokens":474},"totalTokens":6899,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":6284,"completion_tokens":615,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":6272,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":12,"total_tokens":6899,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":6272},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":474}},"reasoningTokens":474,"cachedInputTokens":6272},"ms":6501,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphy1-mcq-np1-004-v3","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"A","working":"The normal force is always perpendicular to the contact surface pointing away from the surface into the object. Since the ball is on the inside of the track at the 3 o'clock position (rightmost point), the surface is to its right, so the normal force pushes horizontally to the left toward the circle's center.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"2.9","required_units":[2],"difficulty":"Easy"},"usage":{"inputTokens":6614,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":6614,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":558,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":160,"reasoningTokens":398},"totalTokens":7172,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":398,"promptTokenCount":6614,"candidatesTokenCount":160,"totalTokenCount":7172,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":6614}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":160}]},"reasoningTokens":398,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":4756,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphy1-mcq-038-v2","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"C","working":"Elastic potential energy is given by U_s = (1/2)k(Δx)^2. Since Δx increases from 0.10 m to 0.30 m (a factor of 3), the potential energy scales by a factor of 3^2 = 9. Thus, the potential energy increases to 9 times its initial value.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"3.3","required_units":[3],"difficulty":"Easy"},"usage":{"inputTokens":6611,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":6611,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":482,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":171,"reasoningTokens":311},"totalTokens":7093,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":311,"promptTokenCount":6611,"candidatesTokenCount":171,"totalTokenCount":7093,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":6611}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":171}]},"reasoningTokens":311,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":6988,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphy1-mcq-np1-009-v2","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"C","working":"The change in kinetic energy is ΔK = 0.5 * m * (v_f^2 - v_i^2) = 0.5 * 800 kg * (20^2 - 10^2) m^2/s^2 = 400 * 300 = 120,000 J. Note that 40,000 J is a classic distractor arising from the incorrect calculation 0.5 * m * (Δv)^2.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"3.1","required_units":[3],"difficulty":"Easy"},"usage":{"inputTokens":6580,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":6580,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":819,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":208,"reasoningTokens":611},"totalTokens":7399,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":611,"promptTokenCount":6580,"candidatesTokenCount":208,"totalTokenCount":7399,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":6580}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":208}]},"reasoningTokens":611,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":6142,"error":""}
{"key":"u13-apphy1-mcq-np1-009-v3","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","sample":1,"ok":true,"label":{"chosen_label":"C","working":"Change in kinetic energy is ΔK = 1/2 * m * (vf^2 - vi^2). Substituting the given values: ΔK = 0.5 * 0.50 kg * ((8 m/s)^2 - (12 m/s)^2) = 0.25 * (64 - 144) = 0.25 * (-80) = -20 J.","more_than_one_defensible_choice":false,"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"primary_topic_code":"3.1","required_units":[3],"difficulty":"Easy"},"usage":{"inputTokens":6566,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":6566,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":580,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":188,"reasoningTokens":392},"totalTokens":7146,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":392,"promptTokenCount":6566,"candidatesTokenCount":188,"totalTokenCount":7146,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":6566}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":188}]},"reasoningTokens":392,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":4508,"error":""}
